2026-09-29): the plan in the store\\n4\\t(attavo/plan.py) orders issues, and the forge holds what the plan does\\n5\\tnot -- each issue's title, whether it is open, when it closed, its\\n6\\tlabels, and, before it has a spec, the paths it claims in a \\\"## Claims\\\"\\n7\\tsection of its body. The product names no vendor: the tenant's command\\n8\\tprints the issues as JSON, one object per issue, and this module reads\\n9\\tit. The claims are parsed here, not by the tenant's command, so every\\n10\\ttenant's issues are read by one rule.\\n11\\t\\n12\\tA read that cannot be made is \\\"not read\\\" with its reason, never an empty\\n13\\tlist: no command in the manifest, a command that exits non-zero or runs\\n14\\tpast its bound, or output that is not the shape below.\\n15\\t\\n16\\t    [{\\\"number\\\": 264, \\\"title\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"state\\\": \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\",\\n17\\t      \\\"closed_at\\\": \\\"<iso>\\\" | null, \\\"labels\\\": [\\\"...\\\"], \\\"body\\\": \\\"...\\\"}]\\n18\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n19\\tfrom __future__ import annotations\\n20\\t\\n21\\timport json\\n22\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\n23\\tfrom typing import Any, TypedDict\\n24\\t\\n25\\tfrom attavo.testtool import run_bounded\\n26\\t\\n27\\tTIMEOUT_S = 60\\n28\\tSTATES = (\\\"open\\\", \\\"closed\\\")\\n29\\t\\n30\\t\\n31\\tclass Issue(TypedDict):\\n32\\t    number: int\\n33\\t    title: str\\n34\\t    state: str\\n35\\t    closed_at: str | None\\n36\\t    labels: list[str]\\n37\\t    claims: list[str] | None\\n38\\t\\n39\\t\\n40\\tdef parse_claims(body: str) -> list[str] | None:\\n41\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The paths under a \\\"## Claims\\\" heading, up to the next \\\"## \\\"\\n42\\t    heading: one \\\"- path\\\" line each. None when the body has no Claims\\n43\\t    section, which is not the same as a section that lists nothing.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n44\\t    lines = body.splitlines()\\n45\\t    starts = [i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.rstrip() == \\\"## Claims\\\"]\\n46\\t    if not 