{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .attavo/bin/forge-check-log; rg -n 'doctor|proof|FAILED|failure|ERROR' attest/records/267/build-03.log | tail -80; rg -n \\\"def .*stop|doctor failure|forge_checks|conclusion.*failure|class.*returned|provenance\\\" /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest -g '*.py' -g 'attavo' | head -240; git diff --stat 243a9c2190795c432fa08662722648349a71ebcf..98cfff8a4c1185376f1f77cbe7cdcef1d0b1ed24; git diff --name-status 243a9c2190795c432fa08662722648349a71ebcf..98cfff8a4c1185376f1f77cbe7cdcef1d0b1ed24; rg -n '\"'^diff --git|issues_command|attavo/issues.py|forge-issues|test_issues|record_schemas'\"' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp2gcq9hfb/diff.patch | head -200\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"forge-check-log: [forge].check_log_command for attavo counsel (issue #175).\n\nTakes a sha and a check name on argv; finds the check run of that name on\nthat sha (gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/<sha>/check-runs) and prints\nthe failed steps' log for the run it points at (gh run view <id>\n--log-failed). Exits non-zero, printing nothing to stdout, when the sha\ncarries no check run of that name, the check names no run the forge's own\nURL scheme exposes, or either gh call fails: attavo counsel appends the\nsha and the check name to this command string and runs it under a shell,\nreading a nonzero exit as \"no log available\" for that check.\n\nWhen a sha carries more than one check run of the same name (a retrigger),\nthe one that actually concluded (not \"skipped\") is preferred, since that\nis the run whose log explains a real stop.\n\nWritten from schema/manifest.schema.json's own description of\n[forge].check_log_command and from `gh`, independently of tenant zero's\nequivalent script.\n\nUsage: forge-check-log <sha> <check-name>\nRequires: `gh`, authenticated, run inside this repository's checkout.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\n\ndef main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    if len(argv) != 2:\n        print(\"usage: forge-check-log <sha> <check-name>\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    sha, name = argv\n    run = subprocess.run(\n        [\"gh\", \"api\", f\"repos/{{owner}}/{{repo}}/commits/{sha}/check-runs?per_page=100\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30, check=False,\n    )\n    if run.returncode != 0:\n        print(run.stderr.strip() or f\"forge-check-log: sha {sha} not found\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    try:\n        payload = json.loads(run.stdout)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        print(f\"forge-check-log: unexpected response for sha {sha}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\n    matches = [c for c in payload.get(\"check_runs\", []) if c.get(\"name\") == name]\n    if not matches:\n        print(f\"forge-check-log: no check named {name!r} on sha {sha}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    check = next((c for c in matches if c.get(\"conclusion\") not in (None, \"skipped\")), matches[0])\n\n    url = check.get(\"html_url\") or check.get(\"details_url\") or \"\"\n    found = re.search(r\"/actions/runs/(\\d+)\", url)\n    if not found:\n        print(f\"forge-check-log: check {name!r} on sha {sha} names no run\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    run_id = found.group(1)\n\n    log = subprocess.run(\n        [\"gh\", \"run\", \"view\", run_id, \"--log-failed\"],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, check=False,\n    )\n    if log.returncode != 0:\n        print(log.stderr.strip() or f\"forge-check-log: no log for run {run_id}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    print(log.stdout, end=\"\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\n1:{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"init\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-267\",\"session_id\":\"f2e0c4f7-36d4-465e-a2fe-27db257201e7\",\"tools\":[\"Bash\",\"CronCreate\",\"CronDelete\",\"CronList\",\"DesignSync\",\"Edit\",\"EnterWorktree\",\"ExitWorktree\",\"ListAgents\",\"NotebookEdit\",\"PushNotification\",\"Read\",\"RemoteTrigger\",\"ReportFindings\",\"SendMessage\",\"Skill\",\"StructuredOutput\",\"TaskStop\",\"ToolSearch\",\"WebFetch\",\"WebSearch\",\"Write\"],\"mcp_servers\":[],\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"permissionMode\":\"default\",\"slash_commands\":[\"code-factory-writing\",\"deep-research\",\"design\",\"design-sync\",\"dataviz\",\"update-config\",\"verify\",\"debug\",\"code-review\",\"simplify\",\"batch\",\"fewer-permission-prompts\",\"doctor\",\"loop\",\"schedule\",\"claude-api\",\"workflow-authoring\",\"run\",\"run-skill-generator\",\"advisor\",\"agents\",\"auto-mode-setup\",\"autocompact\",\"clear\",\"color\",\"compact\",\"config\",\"output-style\",\"context\",\"effort\",\"fast\",\"focus\",\"heapdump\",\"init\",\"mcp\",\"import\",\"model\",\"__remote-workflow\",\"workflow-launch-exec\",\"reload-plugins\",\"reload-skills\",\"rename\",\"ultrareview\",\"security-review\",\"usage-credits\",\"extra-usage\",\"usage\",\"insights\",\"recap\",\"skill-doctor\",\"goal\",\"design-consent\",\"design-revoke\",\"list-agents\",\"team-onboarding\",\"anthropic-skills:code-factory-writing\",\"anthropic-skills:docs\",\"anthropic-skills:docx\",\"anthropic-skills:google-workspace\",\"anthropic-skills:import-memory\",\"anthropic-skills:morning\",\"anthropic-skills:pdf\",\"anthropic-skills:pptx\",\"anthropic-skills:skill-creator\",\"anthropic-skills:write-in-my-voice\",\"anthropic-skills:xlsx\"],\"terminal_slash_commands\":[\"doctor\",\"color\",\"focus\",\"reload-plugins\"],\"apiKeySource\":\"none\",\"claude_code_version\":\"2.1.285\",\"output_style\":\"default\",\"agents\":[\"architect\",\"challenger\",\"claude\",\"cost\",\"data\",\"devops\",\"docs\",\"engineer\",\"Explore\",\"general-purpose\",\"Plan\",\"pm\",\"quality\",\"security\",\"statusline-setup\",\"ux\"],\"skills\":[\"code-factory-writing\",\"deep-research\",\"design\",\"design-sync\",\"dataviz\",\"update-config\",\"verify\",\"debug\",\"code-review\",\"simplify\",\"batch\",\"fewer-permission-prompts\",\"doctor\",\"loop\",\"schedule\",\"claude-api\",\"workflow-authoring\",\"run\",\"run-skill-generator\",\"anthropic-skills:code-factory-writing\",\"anthropic-skills:docs\",\"anthropic-skills:docx\",\"anthropic-skills:google-workspace\",\"anthropic-skills:import-memory\",\"anthropic-skills:morning\",\"anthropic-skills:pdf\",\"anthropic-skills:pptx\",\"anthropic-skills:skill-creator\",\"anthropic-skills:write-in-my-voice\",\"anthropic-skills:xlsx\"],\"plugins\":[{\"name\":\"cc-plugin-agents-md\",\"path\":\"builtin\",\"source\":\"cc-plugin-agents-md@builtin\"},{\"name\":\"cc-plugin-telemetry\",\"path\":\"builtin\",\"source\":\"cc-plugin-telemetry@builtin\"}],\"capabilities\":[\"interrupt_receipt_v1\",\"interrupt_cancel_queued_v1\",\"msg_lifecycle_v1\",\"mcp_read_resource_v1\",\"mcp_tool_ui_meta_v1\"],\"analytics_disabled\":false,\"product_feedback_disabled\":false,\"uuid\":\"5d7971b7-9d18-4724-a879-a0db688e089b\",\"memory_paths\":{\"auto\":\"/Users/davidbean/.claude/projects/-Users-davidbean-Projects-attest/memory/\"},\"messaging_socket_path\":\"/tmp/cc-socks/50587.sock\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"per_turn_effort_active\":false,\"view_mode\":\"default\"}\n7:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01W1H85mtJNeR3DxgRkza1nu\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"attempt build-02 stopped as unclassed: [adapter exited 1]\\nsignature: [adapter exited ]\\n\\nsteer from counsel-02:\\nThe build did not reach the item: the configured Claude Code subscription login again failed because its OAuth session had expired and could not be refreshed. Authentication failures are deliberately not classified as transient vendor-capacity failures, and this changes neither the specification nor the