\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/manifest.schema.json:76:      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The tenant's own definition of done: a whole-tree check, as the tenant runs it locally. attavo build runs it each iteration, after the claims boundary, the criteria, and the selected tests -- pass requires its exit to be 0, and a non-zero exit reaches the executor as feedback. Optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused (unlike [tests], which build requires).\\\",\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_doctor.py:4:fail at the first commit and must fail: that is the definition of done,\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_retry.py:3:reason that does not touch the definition of done is started again by a\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_ledger.py:102:    commit gets exactly one class and the summary counts operator acts 2\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:66:      \\\"description\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"answer\\\\\\\": the stop is answerable inside the rules. \\\\\\\"patch\\\\\\\": the stop is a product defect. \\\\\\\"person\\\\\\\": the answer would touch the definition of done and no rule covers it.\\\"\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:70:      \\\"description\\\": \\\"instruction, mechanism, guard -- each a path and symbol or a ruling id.\\\",\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/schema/records/counsel.schema.json:76:          \\\"kind\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"instruction\\\", \\\"mechanism\\\", \\\"guard\\\"]},\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/README.md:103: \\\"citations\\\": [{\\\"kind\\\": \\\"instruction\\\" | \\\"mechanism\\\" | \\\"guard\\\",\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/README.md:7:`bin/attavo doctor <tenant-root>` is the definition of done. It asserts three proofs and exits non-zero until all three hold:\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_build.py:142:    not the definition of done the spec's claims de